---
description: FastAPI backend rules
globs: backend/**
alwaysApply: false
---

- Python 3.12, fully typed; `mypy --strict app` must pass. Use `uv run` for every command.
- Layers: routers (`app/api`) → services (`app/services`) → repositories (`app/repositories`) → models.
  SQL only in repositories. Routers: parse input, call one service method, return a schema.
- Every route has exactly one auth dependency from `app/core/auth.py`. New public routes need a comment
  explaining why they are public.
- Pydantic v2 schemas for every request and response (`app/schemas`). No `dict` responses for new routes.
- Raise `AppError` subclasses; never `HTTPException` with a raw message.
- Async all the way: SQLAlchemy async sessions, `httpx.AsyncClient` with explicit timeouts.
- Jobs in `app/workers` are idempotent (upsert on natural keys) and safe to retry.
- Migrations: change models → `make migration m="..."` → read the generated file → `make migrate`.
  Never edit an applied migration; add a new one.
- Tests: unit tests need no network; integration tests use `pytestmark = pytest.mark.integration`
  and a real Postgres. Test the unhappy paths (wrong role, expired token, bad cursor).
- Ingestion: only AI summaries are stored, never full article text. Respect each source's terms.
- AI: prompts are versioned files in `app/ai/prompts/`; store `prompt_version` on every post; run
  `validate_summary` before anything auto-publishes.
